    # --- offices, parties and nationality (the probe's own top misses) ---
    #
    # THE OFFICE, NOT THE OFFICEHOLDER. "president" was the most spoken noun in
    # the Nathan Dean master - 29 times - and it had no entry at all, so it was
    # searched LITERALLY. A literal search for "president" returns photographs
    # of identifiable living politicians, which is the single thing this
    # vocabulary exists to prevent, and it had been true of every politics clip
    # this rig has ever cut. Every office below resolves to the BUILDING it
    # works out of, which is a place and cannot be anybody.
    #
    # BOTH PARTIES GET THE SAME PICTURE, and that is the point rather than a
    # shortcut: a polling station is what either word is actually about, and any
    # picture that told them apart would be a picture of partisans.
