    # ========================================================================
    # 2,826 -> 10693 (2026-08-25). THE BIG RUN.
    #
    # The owner: "we need to expand our vocab exponentially more ... I feel like
    # we're using a lot of the same stuff in some of the videos, I don't have the
    # best b-roll. We should ALWAYS have something. Like if it says 'think' -
    # okay, we have a shot for thinking. We need to have a shot for every single
    # word we can think of. This is gonna be a massive run."
    #
    # Fourteen domains written in parallel and merged: abstractions and states of
    # mind, finance, policy, energy, tech and AI, space and defence, health and
    # biotech, science, industry, consumer, work and society, everyday objects
    # and actions, time and weather and place-types.
    #
    # THE HARD PART WAS THE ABSTRACTIONS, and they are the reason the owner asked.
    # A word like "decide" has no photograph, so it gets a physical metaphor a
    # stock library actually holds - a crossroads signpost; "doubt" a forked
    # path; "hesitate" a foot hovering over a stepping stone; "regret" a crumpled
    # letter in a wastebasket. That is a picture of the IDEA, which is what
    # b-roll is for, rather than a picture of the word, which is what a literal
    # search returns.
    #
    # EVERY ENTRY WAS TESTED AGAINST 2,512 REAL SENTENCES BEFORE IT WAS ALLOWED
    # IN, and this is the part that matters. candidates() ranks a word group by
    # (in EXPAND, multi-word, LENGTH), so a LONGER new key BEATS a shorter
    # correct one - which is how the previous pass shipped eleven regressions
    # ("balance" hijacking "balance sheet", "ceiling" hijacking "debt ceiling",
    # "benchmark" beating "yield"). Those were found by a human reading sentences.
    # This time the check is mechanical: the corpus is every transcript this rig
    # has, the pick is computed with and without each candidate, and anything
    # that displaces a CURATED pick is dropped. 8,080 candidates went in, 213
    # were dropped, 7,867 shipped.
    #
    # It only protects a curated pick. When the old answer was the word itself
    # the search was LITERAL - the failure this whole expansion exists to end -
    # so displacing that is the improvement, not the regression.
    #
    # Dropped for cause, as examples of what the gate is for: "pumping" (would
    # have hijacked "gold pumping hard" into an oil pump jack), "possible" (beat
    # "AI"), "expensive" (beat "debt"), "decades" (beat "gold").
